{
 "request_id": "e32372056a9e",
 "question": "Compare the three meanings of 'index' in data wrangling.",
 "answer": "The term 'index' in data wrangling has three meanings, as stated in [S1] and [S2]. In meaning 1, a database index is a data structure that speeds up lookups on a column but makes writes slower [S1]. In meaning 2, these three meanings of the word index are unrelated [S1]. In meaning 3, a database index is a data structure that speeds up lookups on a column but makes writes slower [S1]. All these meanings are supported by the Data Wrangling Handbook, [S1] and the Data Wrangling Glossary, [S2].",
